{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Solution {\n    static Scanner sc;\n    static PrintWriter out;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        \n        int a = sc.nextInt();\n        int b = sc.nextInt();\n        int l = sc.nextInt() - 1;\n        int r = sc.nextInt() - 1;\n        int segmentLength = r - l + 1;\n        \n        int minDistinct = segmentLength;\n        \n        for (char c1 = 'a'; c1 <= 'z'; c1++) {\n            for (char c2 = 'a'; c2 <= 'z'; c2++) {\n                for (char c3 = 'a'; c3 <= 'z'; c3++) {\n                    char[] p = {c1, c2, c3};\n                    minDistinct = Math.min(minDistinct, evaluateSegment(a, b, l, r, p));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        out.println(minDistinct);\n        out.flush();\n    }\n\n    static int evaluateSegment(int a, int b, int L, int R, char[] pattern) {\n        int period = a + b;\n        char[] full = new char[3 * period];\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n            System.arraycopy(buildPrefix(a, full, i * period), 0, full, i * period, a);\n            Arrays.fill(full, i * period + a, (i + 1) * period, pattern[i]);\n        }\n        \n        int start = L % period;\n        int len = R - L + 1;\n        char[] window = new char[len];\n        System.arraycopy(full, start, window, 0, Math.min(len, full.length - start));\n        \n        boolean[] seen = new boolean[26];\n        for (char c : window) {\n            seen[c - 'a'] = true;\n        }\n        \n        int count = 0;\n        for (boolean b : seen) if (b) count++;\n        return count;\n    }\n\n    static char[] buildPrefix(int len, char[] buffer, int idx) {\n        boolean[] used = new boolean[26];\n        for (int i = idx - 1; i >= idx - len && i >= 0; i--) {\n            used[buffer[i] - 'a'] = true;\n        }\n        \n        char[] result = new char[len];\n        char cur = 'a';\n        for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n            while (used[cur - 'a']) cur++;\n            result[i] = cur++;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n\n    static class Scanner {\n        BufferedReader reader;\n        StringTokenizer tokenizer;\n\n        public Scanner(InputStream stream) {\n            reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(stream));\n        }\n\n        String next() throws IOException {\n            while (tokenizer == null || !tokenizer.hasMoreTokens()) {\n                tokenizer = new StringTokenizer(reader.readLine());\n            }\n            return tokenizer.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() throws IOException {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() throws IOException {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() throws IOException {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport io\nimport itertools\n\ndef build_prefix(len_, buffer, idx):\n    used = [False] * 26\n    for i in range(idx - 1, idx - len_ - 1, -1):\n        if i >= 0:\n            used[buffer[i] - ord('a')] = True\n    \n    result = []\n    cur = ord('a')\n    for _ in range(len_):\n        while used[cur - ord('a')]:\n            cur += 1\n        result.append(chr(cur))\n        cur += 1\n    return result\n\ndef evaluate_segment(a, b, L, R, pattern):\n    period = a + b\n    full = [''] * (3 * period)\n    \n    for i in range(3):\n        prefix = build_prefix(a, full, i * period)\n        for j in range(a):\n            full[i * period + j] = prefix[j]\n        for j in range(a, period):\n            full[i * period + j] = pattern[i]\n    \n    start = L % period\n    length = R - L + 1\n    window = []\n    for i in range(length):\n        if start + i < len(full):\n            window.append(full[start + i])\n        else:\n            window.append(full[(start + i) % len(full)])\n    \n    seen = [False] * 26\n    for c in window:\n        seen[ord(c) - ord('a')] = True\n    \n    count = sum(seen)\n    return count\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    a = int(input_data[0])\n    b = int(input_data[1])\n    l = int(input_data[2]) - 1\n    r = int(input_data[3]) - 1\n    segment_length = r - l + 1\n    \n    min_distinct = segment_length\n    \n    for c1 in range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1):\n        for c2 in range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1):\n            for c3 in range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1):\n                pattern = [chr(c1), chr(c2), chr(c3)]\n                min_distinct = min(min_distinct, evaluate_segment(a, b, l, r, pattern))\n    \n    print(min_distinct)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.125868119648658e-05, -7.15